## Summary

Adds a bulk senior-squad registration workflow to the shared-world manager portal.

## Manager experience

- replaces the one-player registration card with a complete senior-roster checklist;
- preselects the currently registered senior squad;
- excludes players aged 21 or younger, who remain youth-eligible;
- shows player name, position, age and TBG rating;
- provides **Select best available** and **Restore current** controls;
- submits the complete selected senior squad in one manager action;
- reports whether changes were queued or the submitted roster was already current.

## Canonical workflow

- adds an authenticated `bulk-squad-registration` endpoint;
- validates the active manager appointment and canonical club ownership;
- enforces the canonical registration limit;
- submits the entire roster through one transactional `submit_bulk_registration_commands` RPC;
- incorporates the latest pending registration/removal intent before deciding which superseding commands are required;
- restores a reselected player even when an older pending removal exists;
- submits removals before additions so a full 25-player roster can be changed safely;
- rolls the whole batch back if any command submission fails;
- uses one stable batch ID and deterministic per-player request keys;
- routes every resulting change through `submit_manager_world_command`, preserving PR #115 supersession, audit, inbox and idempotency behaviour.

## Tests

Regression coverage verifies:

- roster-diff calculation;
- registration-limit enforcement;
- rejection of unowned players;
- youth exclusion;
- preservation of current selection;
- pending-command reconciliation;
- one transactional batch RPC with removal-before-addition ordering;
- portal asset loading and canonical RPC wiring.

## Deployment

Run the new Supabase migration after merge:

`supabase/migrations/20260725_pr116_atomic_bulk_registration.sql`

Refs #93
